            <ArticleTitle>A tool for more accurate risk-prediction in acute coronary syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>22-3, 13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Standardized guidelines are fine, but one size does not fit all when it comes to cardiac patients. In fact, clinicians often struggle with deciding how aggressively to treat a patient who has suffered a heart attack or another form of acute coronary syndrome. However, a new risk-prediction tool can help guide clinicians to more precise conclusions regarding patient care.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
